; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; CAL probe tip on a gauge pin (or any round boss) of known diameter
; #3034: measures the probe's calibration offset #3032 from outside, the
; counterpart of o<probe_cal_round_pocket> in a ring. The probe starts
; above the pin's centre, within #3020 of its top. It touches the top, then
; measures across X and Y from outside twice (step out #3034/2 + #3023,
; plunge #3021 + tip diameter + #3022 below the clearance height, touch
; towards the pin, rise; the second pass, from the refined centre, counts)
; with the tool table's tip diameter and no calibration offset. The offset
; is #3032 = (#3034 - measured width) / 2, signed, so the effective tip
; radius #5410/2 - #3032 equals the true one: per axis averaged (#3036 =
; 0), X only (1) or Y only (2). Reports z_minus_probed_position #1009,
; x_probed_width #1001, x_center_probed #1002, y_probed_width #1003,
; y_center_probed #1004, averaged_diam #1010 (all uncalibrated) and, last
; and only once, calibration_offset_3032 with the new value, which ferrum
; saves. Never writes a work offset, whatever #3030 says. Ends over the
; pin's centre at the clearance height.
o<probe_cal_boss> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_cal_boss> return
o10 endif
o<ferrum_probe_ready> call
M73
M50 P0
G90 G94
o20 if [#3034 LE 0]
    (ABORT, Set the gauge pin diameter #3034 first)
o20 endif
o21 if [[#3036 LT 0] OR [#3036 GT 2]]
    (ABORT, Cal axis #3036 must be 0 X+Y, 1 X or 2 Y)
o21 endif

o<ferrum_touch> call [2] [-1] [#3020]
#1009 = #<_ferrum_hit>
#<z_clear> = [#1009 + #3021]
#<z_probe> = [#1009 - #5410 - #3022]
o<ferrum_guarded_move> call [0] [0] [#<z_clear> - #5422]

o<ferrum_span_outside> call [0] [#3034] [#<z_clear>] [#<z_probe>] [1]
o<ferrum_span_outside> call [1] [#3034] [#<z_clear>] [#<z_probe>] [1]
o<ferrum_span_outside> call [0] [#3034] [#<z_clear>] [#<z_probe>] [1]
#1001 = #<_ferrum_width>
#1002 = #<_ferrum_center>
o<ferrum_span_outside> call [1] [#3034] [#<z_clear>] [#<z_probe>] [1]
#1003 = #<_ferrum_width>
#1004 = #<_ferrum_center>
#1010 = [[#1001 + #1003] / 2]

#<ex> = [[#3034 - #1001] / 2]
#<ey> = [[#3034 - #1003] / 2]
o30 if [#3036 EQ 1]
    #<cal> = #<ex>
o30 elseif [#3036 EQ 2]
    #<cal> = #<ey>
o30 else
    #<cal> = [[#<ex> + #<ey>] / 2]
o30 endif
o40 if [#<cal> GE [#5410 / 2]]
    (ABORT, Calibration gives no usable tip radius - check #3034 and the tip diameter)
o40 endif
#3032 = #<cal>

(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"z_minus_probed_position"}.setValue{#1009}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"x_probed_width"}.setValue{#1001}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"x_center_probed"}.setValue{#1002}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"y_probed_width"}.setValue{#1003}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"y_center_probed"}.setValue{#1004}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"averaged_diam"}.setValue{#1010}])
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"calibration_offset_3032"}.setValue{#3032}])
G90
o<probe_cal_boss> endsub
M2
